-- title:
--   Order elements of reduced norm divisible by r approximating Pi
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, rationals $a,b$, and a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$ of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and it is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Assume moreover that the image of every integer lies in $\Lambda$. Let $\mathrm{coord}:\Lambda\to Z_r\times Z_r$, where $Z_r$ denotes the Witt vectors `WittVector r (GaloisField r 2)` of the field with $r^2$ elements, satisfy `IsOrderCoord Λ r coord`: $\mathrm{coord}$ is additive and injective, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, is multiplicative in the twisted sense $\mathrm{coord}(mm')=(\alpha\alpha'+r\,\beta\,\sigma(\beta'),\ \alpha\beta'+\beta\,\sigma(\alpha'))$ with $\sigma$ the Witt vector Frobenius, has $r$-adically dense image (every pair of residues modulo $r^k$ is attained), and satisfies $\alpha_m+\sigma(\alpha_m)=n$ whenever $m+\bar m=n$ with $n\in\mathbb{Z}$. Then for every $k\in\mathbb{N}$ there exists $m\in\Lambda$ such that $m\,\bar m$ is the image of $r\,n$ for some integer $n$, and such that $(\mathrm{coord}\,m)_1$ and $(\mathrm{coord}\,m)_2-1$ both lie in the ideal of $Z_r$ generated by $r^k$.
--
--   The elements produced lie in the two-sided prime of $\Lambda$ above the ramified prime $r$ and are $r$-adically close to a uniformiser $\Pi$ of the maximal order of the quaternion division algebra over $\mathbb{Q}_r$; approximating $\Pi$ inside the global order in this way is what allows global quaternionic elements to implement the Frobenius, resp. Atkin–Lehner, action in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation. It is used in the rigidification statements [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.isPiTranslate_of_isRigTransport_of_corr_relFrobenius_of_isAtkinLehnerQuotientVia`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.isPiTranslate_of_isRigTransport_of_corr_relFrobenius_of_isAtkinLehnerQuotientVia) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.span_range_eq_span_range_varpi_of_isAtkinLehnerQuotientVia_of_forall_comp_eq_apply_nilEval`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.span_range_eq_span_range_varpi_of_isAtkinLehnerQuotientVia_of_forall_comp_eq_apply_nilEval).
